WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.480
Rhiannon: There are times when everyone
feels the strain and Covid 19 has

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.980
affected all of us in some way, either
through being in lockdown or losing a

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.059
friend or family member to the virus.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.969
For children and young people however,
the changes have been really dramatic

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.479
challenging everything they’ve grown
to understand to be normal in life.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:24.240
Leah: Some children and young people
may have enjoyed not going to school,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.150
while others will have really struggled
with the coronavirus outbreak keeping

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.959
them at home and away from friends.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.880
Others may be coming to terms with
family problems, loss or changes to

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.499
their living situation and not being able
to see family members for a long time.

00:00:37.499 --> 00:00:37.599
Rhiannon: Having to self-isolate,
due to a class or school outbreak

00:00:37.599 --> 00:00:40.173
or periods of school closures have
created many uncertainties to many

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:40.688
children and young people about
their education and their futures.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:51.911
Leah: Coronavirus has impacted
everyone in many different ways

00:00:51.911 --> 00:00:56.400
and mental health is one of those.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:01.850
This pandemic can be seen as a medical
crisis now but also a mental health crisis

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:06.320
going forward and will have a great impact
on the mental health of many children

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:08.080
and young people in the years to come.

